            "text": "Perfectly equal love need not entail identical treatment when recipients possess different histories, vulnerabilities, and modes of understanding. A disclosure calibrated to one person might overwhelm another, be dismissed by a third, or produce dependence rather than mature trust. Individualized timing can therefore be interpreted as an accommodation rather than neglect, provided the route remains genuinely available and proportionate. This defense improves upon bare possibility by imposing conditions: disclosure must progress, burdens cannot exceed the seeker's capacities, and delay must connect intelligibly to the relationship's development rather than remain indefinitely opaque."
