          "text": "Independent evidential domains can reinforce one another when the conclusion of one narrows the live explanations in another. A necessary personal source would make objective moral authority less ad hoc, while a historically situated revelation would identify the otherwise generic source. The case should therefore test conditional dependence: cosmology cannot count twice as resurrection evidence, but moral and historical data may become more intelligible after a personal creator is independently plausible."
